{"type":"message","id":"5576e1f9","parentId":"f3032904","timestamp":"2026-02-13T08:05:19.218Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_lstra5a540k6_2","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 6205 bytes to /Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/restore_database.sh"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770969919213}}
{"type":"message","id":"9c0101cb","parentId":"5576e1f9","timestamp":"2026-02-13T08:05:19.239Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_lstra5a540k6_3","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 2944 bytes to /Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/run_backup.sh"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770969919236}}
{"type":"message","id":"fe531696","parentId":"9c0101cb","timestamp":"2026-02-13T08:06:14.881Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me create the cron setup, environment template, and documentation.","thinkingSignature":"9f224850ad143562e55355bf45144fab787177c6991dc1e23e1cc7ea9952f1ff"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pdmxp3bx645q_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"#!/bin/bash\n#\n# Generate crontab entries for database backups\n# Run this script to install/update the backup cron schedule\n#\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nBACKUP_SCRIPT=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/run_backup.sh\"\nVERIFY_SCRIPT=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/verify_backups.sh\"\n\n# Create crontab entries\nCRON_ENTRIES=\"# Database Backup Cron Schedule\n# Generated by backup_setup.sh\n\n# Full backup - Daily at 2:00 AM\n0 2 * * * ${BACKUP_SCRIPT} full >> ${SCRIPT_DIR}/logs/cron_backup.log 2>&1\n\n# Incremental backup - Every 6 hours\n0 */6 * * * ${BACKUP_SCRIPT} incremental >> ${SCRIPT_DIR}/logs/cron_backup.log 2>&1\n\n# Backup verification - Daily at 6:00 AM\n0 6 * * * ${VERIFY_SCRIPT} >> ${SCRIPT_DIR}/logs/cron_verify.log 2>&1\n\n# Monthly full backup retention cleanup - 1st day of month at 3:00 AM\n0 3 1 * * find ${SCRIPT_DIR}/../* -name \\\"*.log\\\" -mtime +90 -delete\n\"\n\n# Output crontab entries\necho \"$CRON_ENTRIES\"\n\n# Optionally install (uncomment to enable)\n# echo \"$CRON_ENTRIES\" | crontab -\n\necho \"\"\necho \"To install these crontab entries, run:\"\necho \"  ./backup_setup.sh | crontab -\"\necho \"\"\necho \"Or add manually to your crontab:\"\necho \"  crontab -e\"\n","file_path":"/Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/backup_setup.sh"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pdmxp3bx645q_2","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Database Backup Environment Template\n# Copy this file to .backup.env and fill in the values\n#\n\n# ============================================\n# Database Configuration (Required)\n# ============================================\n# Get DATABASE_URL from Supabase dashboard:\n# Settings > Database > Connection string\nDATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://[user]:[password]@[host]:[port]/[database]\"\n\n# Or individual settings:\n# DB_HOST=\"your-project.supabase.co\"\n# DB_PORT=\"5432\"\n# DB_NAME=\"postgres\"\n# DB_USER=\"postgres\"\n# DB_PASSWORD=\"your-password\"\n\n# ============================================\n# Backup Storage\n# ============================================\nBACKUP_DIR=\"/Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups\"\nBACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30\nBACKUP_RETENTION_WEEKLY=8\nBACKUP_RETENTION_MONTHLY=12\n\n# ============================================\n# S3 Remote Storage (Optional)\n# ============================================\n# For AWS S3:\nS3_ENABLED=false\nS3_BUCKET=\"your-backup-bucket\"\nS3_REGION=\"us-east-1\"\nS3_ACCESS_KEY=\"your-access-key\"\nS3_SECRET_KEY=\"your-secret-key\"\nS3_PREFIX=\"database\"\n\n# For S3-compatible storage (MinIO, DigitalOcean, etc.):\n# S3_ENDPOINT=\"s3.amazonaws.com\"  # or custom endpoint\n\n# ============================================\n# Encryption (Recommended)\n# ============================================\nENCRYPT_BACKUPS=true\n# Generate a strong encryption key:\n#   openssl rand -base64 32\nENCRYPTION_KEY_FILE=\"/Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/config/backup.key\"\n# GPG recipient for backup encryption (optional, alternative to key file)\n# GPG_RECIPIENT=\"backup@example.com\"\n\n# ============================================\n# Backup Types\n# ============================================\nENABLE_FULL_BACKUP=true\nENABLE_INCREMENTAL=false  # Requires WAL archiving configuration\n\n# ============================================\n# Monitoring & Alerts\n# ============================================\n# Slack webhook (optional):\n# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=\"https://hooks.slack.com/services/xxx/yyy/zzz\"\n\n# Email alerts (optional):\n# EMAIL_ALERT_RECIPIENT=\"admin@example.com\"\n\n# Healthcheck.io (optional):\n# HEALTHCHECK_URL=\"https://hc-ping.com/your-uuid\"\n\n# ============================================\n# Scheduling\n# ============================================\nBACKUP_HOUR=2\nBACKUP_MINUTE=0\nFULL_BACKUP_DAY=0  # 0=Sunday, 1=Monday, etc.\n\n# ============================================\n# Verification\n# ============================================\nVERIFY_BACKUPS=true\nRESTORE_TEST_DAYS=7  # Test restore every N days\n","file_path":"/Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/.env.example"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pdmxp3bx645q_3","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# PostgreSQL Database Backup Procedures\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document describes the backup and restore procedures for the PostgreSQL database used in this project.\n\n## Backup Strategy\n\n### Backup Types\n\n| Type | Frequency | Retention | Use Case |\n|------|-----------|-----------|----------|\n| Full Backup | Daily (2:00 AM) | 30 days | Complete database snapshot |\n| Incremental | Every 6 hours | 7 days | Point-in-time recovery |\n| WAL Archives | Continuous | 30 days | Point-in-time recovery |\n\n### Retention Policy\n\n- **Daily backups**: Keep last 30 days\n- **Weekly backups**: Keep last 8 weeks\n- **Monthly backups**: Keep last 12 months\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### 1. Install Required Tools\n\n```bash\n# PostgreSQL client tools\nbrew install postgresql  # macOS\nsudo apt-get install postgresql-client  # Ubuntu/Debian\n\n# AWS CLI (for S3 uploads)\nbrew install awscli\npip install awscli\n```\n\n### 2. Configure Environment\n\n```bash\n# Copy environment template\ncp backups/.env.example backups/.env\n\n# Edit with your settings\nnano backups/.env\n\n# Generate encryption key\nopenssl rand -base64 32 > backups/config/backup.key\nchmod 600 backups/config/backup.key\n```\n\n### 3. Database Connection Test\n\n```bash\n# Test connection to Supabase\nexport DATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db\"\npsql \"$DATABASE_URL\" -c \"SELECT 1;\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running Backups\n\n```bash\n# Run full backup\n./backups/scripts/backup_full.sh\n\n# Run incremental backup\n./backups/scripts/backup_incremental.sh\n\n# Run orchestrated backup (decides based on day)\n./backups/scripts/run_backup.sh full\n./backups/scripts/run_backup.sh incremental\n```\n\n### Listing Backups\n\n```bash\n./backups/scripts/restore_database.sh --list-backups\n```\n\n### Restoring Database\n\n```bash\n# Restore latest backup\n./backups/scripts/restore_database.sh --latest\n\n# Restore specific backup\n./backups/scripts/restore_database.sh full_backup_mydb_20260115_020000.dump.gpg\n\n# Drop existing and restore\n./backups/scripts/restore_database.sh --latest --drop-existing\n\n# Skip checksum verification (not recommended)\n./backups/scripts/restore_database.sh backup.dump --skip-verify\n```\n\n### Verifying Backups\n\n```bash\n# Quick verification (checksums only)\n./backups/scripts/verify_backups.sh\n\n# Full verification with test restore\n./backups/scripts/verify_backups.sh --full-restore-test\n```\n\n## Scheduling with Cron\n\n### Install Cron Jobs\n\n```bash\n# Generate and install crontab\n./backups/scripts/backup_setup.sh | crontab -\n\n# Or manually edit crontab\ncrontab -e\n```\n\n### Cron Schedule\n\n```cron\n# Full backup - Daily at 2:00 AM\n0 2 * * * /Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/run_backup.sh full\n\n# Incremental backup - Every 6 hours\n0 */6 * * * /Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/run_backup.sh incremental\n\n# Verification - Daily at 6:00 AM\n0 6 * * * /Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/scripts/verify_backups.sh\n```\n\n## S3 Configuration\n\n### AWS S3 Setup\n\n1. Create S3 bucket with appropriate encryption\n2. Configure bucket policy for access\n3. Create IAM user with S3 access\n\n### Bucket Policy Example\n\n```json\n{\n    \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n    \"Statement\": [\n        {\n            \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n            \"Principal\": {\n                \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:user/backup-user\"\n            },\n            \"Action\": [\n                \"s3:PutObject\",\n                \"s3:GetObject\",\n                \"s3:DeleteObject\"\n            ],\n            \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::your-backup-bucket/*\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### Lifecycle Policy\n\nSet up S3 lifecycle to move older backups to Glacier:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"Rules\": [\n        {\n            \"ID\": \"Archive old backups\",\n            \"Status\": \"Enabled\",\n            \"Filter\": {\n                \"Prefix\": \"database/\"\n            },\n            \"Transitions\": [\n                {\n                    \"Days\": 30,\n                    \"StorageClass\": \"STANDARD_IA\"\n                },\n                {\n                    \"Days\": 90,\n                    \"StorageClass\": \"GLACIER\"\n                }\n            ],\n            \"Expiration\": {\n                \"Days\": 365\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n## Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR)\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n1. WAL archiving must be enabled\n2. Base backups must be available\n3. Target recovery point must be within retention\n\n### Recovery Process\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stop the application\n# 2. Preserve current data directory\nmv /var/lib/postgresql/data /var/lib/postgresql/data.old\n\n# 3. Create recovery.conf\ncat > /var/lib/postgresql/data/recovery.conf\nrestore_command = 'cp /wal/%f %p'\nrecovery_target_time = '2026-01-15 10:00:00 UTC'\n\n# 4. Start PostgreSQL\n# PostgreSQL will automatically recover to the specified point\n```\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n### Encryption\n\n- All backups are encrypted with AES-256\n- Encryption key stored separately from backups\n- Consider using AWS KMS for key management\n\n### Access Control\n\n- Restrict backup directory permissions: `chmod 700 backups/`\n- Limit database user permissions to backup role\n- Use IAM roles instead of access keys where possible\n\n### Audit Logging\n\n- All backup operations are logged to `backups/logs/`\n- Logs are retained for 90 days\n- Failed backups trigger Slack/email alerts\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n#### \"Connection refused\" errors\n\n```bash\n# Check database is running\npg_isready -h $DB_HOST -p $DB_PORT\n\n# Verify credentials\npsql \"$DATABASE_URL\" -c \"SELECT version();\"\n```\n\n#### \"Permission denied\" errors\n\n```bash\n# Check backup directory permissions\nls -la backups/\n\n# Fix permissions\nchmod 700 backups/config/\nchmod 600 backups/config/backup.key\n```\n\n#### \"No space left on device\"\n\n```bash\n# Check disk space\ndf -h\n\n# Clean up old backups\n./backups/scripts/cleanup.sh\n```\n\n### Getting Help\n\n1. Check logs: `tail -f backups/logs/*.log`\n2. Verify config: `source backups/config/backup.conf && echo $DATABASE_URL`\n3. Test connection: `pg_isready -h $DB_HOST -p $DB_PORT -U $DB_USER`\n\n## Disaster Recovery Plan\n\n### RTO (Recovery Time Objective): 4 hours\n### RPO (Recovery Point Objective): 6 hours\n\n### Recovery Steps\n\n1. **Assess damage** - Determine extent of data loss\n2. **Prepare environment** - Ensure database server is ready\n3. **Restore latest backup** - Follow restore procedures\n4. **Verify integrity** - Run verification scripts\n5. **Resume operations** - Restart application\n\n### Emergency Contacts\n\n- Database Admin: [Your Name]\n- Cloud Provider: [Support Contact]\n","file_path":"/Users/yu-ga/.clawdbot/agents/monetize-agent/backups/RESTORE_PROCEDURES.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.1","usage":{"input":11531,"output":2688,"cacheRead":8465,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22684,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770969919239}}
